            <ArticleTitle>Combined anterior and inferior ST segment elevation during the exercise stress testing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>490-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Exercise induced ST elevation, especially in anterior derivations, does localize the ischemic region. We describe a patient who presented with exercise induced ST elevation in both anterior and inferior leads without prior myocardial infarction. Coronary angiography showed a &quot;wrap around LAD&quot; with significant proximal lesion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
